    explanationWalkthrough:
      'The argument\u2019s core move is causal: ban enacted, litter fell, therefore the ban worked. Every causal claim from a before-and-after comparison assumes that nothing else relevant changed in between. That assumption is exactly what the correct choice probes — a volunteer cleanup launched around the same time would be a rival explanation for cleaner water, and knowing about it would directly affect how much credit the ban deserves. The distractors each miss the causal question. Resident approval bears on the recommendation that neighbors adopt bans, but not on whether Riverton\u2019s ban caused the drop. The pre-ban plastic share is tempting because baselines sound scientific, yet a 40-percent decline is a 40-percent decline regardless of the starting share — it doesn\u2019t test the causal link. The number of neighboring towns and the price of paper bags are simply off-topic for the causation question.',
