    explanationWalkthrough:
      'Structure the principle: the default duty is disclosure; the "unless" clause creates exactly one exception — the patient\u2019s explicit statement that they do not want to hear the risks. Silence, unfamiliarity, or the doctor\u2019s own judgment do not trigger the exception; only an explicit refusal does. Now test each doctor. Chen discloses to a patient who wants full information — duty satisfied. Osei withholds, but at the patient\u2019s explicit request — the exception applies, so no violation. Kim discloses to a patient who said "tell me everything" — duty satisfied. Patel withholds from a patient who "had never discussed the topic" — the exception\u2019s trigger (an explicit refusal) never occurred, so the default duty stood and was breached: a violation. Rao\u2019s patient refused all treatment, so there is no proposed treatment whose risks require disclosure — the duty never arises.',
