      'In a six-month trial, patients who used the Cefalyne headband reported 40 percent fewer migraine days than a control group that received no treatment. The headband delivers mild electrical pulses that the manufacturer says calm overactive nerves. Researchers concluded that the pulses reduce migraine frequency.',
